.TH "HTMLTEXTAREAELEMENT.SELECTIONSTART" "3JS" "September 1, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
HTMLTextAreaElement.selectionStart \- HTMLTextAreaElement:
selectionStart property
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]selectionStart\f[B]\f[R] property of the
\f[CR]HTMLTextAreaElement\f[R] interface specifies the start position of
the current text selection in a \f[CR]<textarea>\f[R] element.
.SH VALUE
A non\-negative number.
.SH DESCRIPTION
The \f[CR]selectionStart\f[R] property is a number representing the
zero\-based index of the first selected character in a
\f[CR]<textarea>\f[R].
The property can be used to retrieve or set the start position.
.PP
When nothing is selected, the value of both \f[CR]selectionStart\f[R]
and \f[CR]selectionEnd\f[R] is the position of the cursor (caret) inside
the \f[CR]<textarea>\f[R] element.
.PP
Setting \f[CR]selectionStart\f[R] to a value greater than the current
value of \f[CR]selectionEnd\f[R] updates both properties to the new
value.
Values greater than the \f[CR]textLength\f[R] are treated as
\f[CR]textLength\f[R].
.PP
The property value can be retrieved and set without the
\f[CR]<textarea>\f[R] having focus, but the element must have focus for
the \f[CR]::selection\f[R] pseudo\-element to match the selected text.
.PP
Setting \f[CR]selectionStart\f[R] to a new value fires the
\f[CR]selectionchange\f[R] and \f[CR]select\f[R] events.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Basic usage
This example reports the selected text and its start and end positions.
Select some text in the textarea, and then click the button.
.SS HTML
.IP
.EX
<\f[B]label\f[R] for=\(dqtext\-box\(dq>Select some text:</\f[B]label\f[R]>
<\f[B]textarea\f[R] id=\(dqtext\-box\(dq rows=\(dq3\(dq>The quick brown fox.</\f[B]textarea\f[R]>
<\f[B]button\f[R] id=\(dqshow\-selection\(dq type=\(dqbutton\(dq>Show selection</\f[B]button\f[R]>
<\f[B]p\f[R] id=\(dqoutput\(dq>No selection reported yet.</\f[B]p\f[R]>
.EE
.SS JavaScript
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] textBox = document.querySelector(\(dq#text\-box\(dq);
\f[B]const\f[R] output = document.querySelector(\(dq#output\(dq);

document.querySelector(\(dq#show\-selection\(dq).addEventListener(\(dqclick\(dq, () \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  \f[B]const\f[R] start = textBox.selectionStart;
  \f[B]const\f[R] end = textBox.selectionEnd;
  \f[B]const\f[R] selectedText = textBox.value.substring(start, end);

  output.textContent = \(gaYou selected \(dq${selectedText}\(dq (start: ${start}, end: ${end}).\(ga;
});
.EE
.SS Result
